The Level 0 Data Flow Diagram (Context Diagram) of the Zariya Fashion Store System shows how the system interacts with two external entities: User (Customer) and Admin.

1. User (Customer) → Zariya Fashion Store System
The customer provides the following information to the system:

Registration / Login – The customer creates an account or logs into the system.

Product Search – The customer searches and browses available fashion products.

Place Order – The customer selects products and places an order.

2. Zariya Fashion Store System → User (Customer)
The system provides the following information to the customer:

Product Details – Information about products such as name, price, size, and description.

Cart Information – Details of products added to the shopping cart.

Order Confirmation – Confirmation after the order is successfully placed.

3. Admin → Zariya Fashion Store System
The Admin interacts with the system to:

Manage Products – Add, update, or delete products.

Manage Orders – View and update customer orders.

View Reports – Access information and reports related to products and orders.

4. Zariya Fashion Store System → Admin
The system provides the Admin with:

Product Data – Details of available products.

Order Data – Information about customer orders.

Reports – System-generated information related to products and orders.
